    question: 'Explain hypothesis testing and confidence intervals with an A/B test. Why is the central limit theorem important?',
    answer:
      '**A/B test:** A = 400/4000 (10%), B = 480/4000 (12%).\n\n**Hypothesis testing steps:**\n1. H0: dono rates barabar · H1: B better\n2. α = 0.05\n3. Test: two-proportion z-test\n4. z ≈ 2.9 → p ≈ 0.004\n5. p < α → H0 reject, significant\n\n**Confidence interval:** lift ka 95% CI ≈ 0.6% se 3.4% — poora positive, matlab improvement real lagta hai. CI p-value se better kyunki effect ka size aur precision dono dikhata hai.\n\n**Central limit theorem:** sample size badhne par sample mean ka distribution normal ho jaata hai (population normal ho ya na ho); isi wajah se z-test/t-test aur CI ke formulas valid hain. Practically n ≥ 30 par approximation theek chalta hai.\n\n| Concept | Kya batata hai | Value |\n|---|---|---|\n| p-value | Chance ka role | 0.004 |\n| CI | Effect ka range | +0.6% to +3.4% |\n| CLT | Test kyun valid | mean ~ normal |\n\n**Exam line:** statistics do kaam karti hai — effect real hai ya nahi (test) aur kitna bada hai (CI).',
